From b337473805809dc6d63f15480cd6a64a4fb96dce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:57:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] v2: remove ZeroMQ from documentation and packaging

Follow the source removal through the documentation, packaging and CI
definitions.

- Delete doc/zmq.md and the contrib/zmq/zmq_sub.py example, and their
  links and packaging entries.
- Drop ZeroMQ from the build instructions, the dependency table, the
  functional-test prerequisites (its naming examples now use
  interface_http.py), Debian/AUR/Docker package lists and the Bookworm
  dependency installer.
- Guix: stop passing -DBUILD_ZMQ=OFF to the source-package configure.
- TeamCity: remove the build-without-zmq configuration and the qemu
  workaround that disabled ZeroMQ for the aarch64 cross build.
- Release note: ZeroMQ is removed; use Chronik's WebSocket for push.

Tier: V2

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Native Qt/ZeroMQ dependency removal preserves new HTTP2/nghttp2 feature flags, helper configuration and OpenSSL3.5 chain; no removed Qt/ZMQ code is restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.
